format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

lesson alpha-beta-gamma
title: Alpha, beta and gamma
minutes: 5
xp: 50
teaches: u2-particle-or-wave
teaches: u2-recognise-radiation
relies_on: u2-parent-daughter

description:
    When a nucleus changes, something comes out. You will meet the three kinds, alpha, beta and gamma, and learn that they are three different things.

cite ref-epa-radioactive-decay
supports: Alpha particles are two protons and two neutrons; gamma rays are photons, weightless packets of energy.

cite ref-openstax-chem-21-3
supports: An alpha particle removes two protons and two neutrons from the parent nucleus.

card c01
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l2-predict-release
scored: 0

card c02
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Three things can come out
figure: three-kinds
figure_at: 1

body:
    When a nucleus changes, it can release [[alpha-particle|alpha]] particles, [[beta-particle|beta]] particles or [[gamma-ray|gamma]] rays. They are three different things. Alpha and beta are particles. Gamma is not.

card c03
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Alpha: a chunk
figure: alpha-figure
figure_at: 1

body:
    An alpha particle is made of 2 protons and 2 neutrons stuck together. It is the nucleus of a helium atom, with no electrons. It is a big, chunky particle.

card c04
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l2-choice-alpha
connected: true

card c05
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Beta: a fast electron
figure: beta-figure
figure_at: 2

body:
    A beta particle is a fast-moving particle released in some decays. In the basic picture, it is a fast electron. It is far lighter than an alpha particle.

card c06
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Gamma: not a particle
figure: gamma-figure
figure_at: 2

body:
    Gamma radiation is not a particle. It is [[electromagnetic-radiation|electromagnetic radiation]], like light but far more energetic. Light is electromagnetic radiation too.

card c07
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l2-match-kinds

card c08
kind: sim
type: radiation-id
scored: 0
task: Read each clue and pick the kind of radiation. Then watch it leave.
hint: Think about what each kind is made of.

