card c15
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: what changes
figure: what-changes
figure_at: 1

body:
    Alpha and beta change the make-up of the nucleus, so a different nucleus is left. In beta decay a neutron changes into a proton and an electron is emitted, along with a tiny particle left out here. Gamma releases extra energy and changes neither the protons nor the neutrons.
